# Performance and Optimization Rules

## Performance Best Practices

- Use lazy loading for heavy operations
- Minimize memory usage and avoid memory leaks
- Avoid blocking the main thread with synchronous operations
- Use webpack for optimal bundling and tree shaking
- Implement proper cleanup in deactivate function

## VSCode Extension Performance

- Use proper activation events to optimize startup time
- Cache expensive operations when possible
- Use disposable patterns for resource management
- Avoid unnecessary API calls
- Use debouncing for user input handling

## Code Optimization

- Prefer const over let, avoid var
- Use async/await instead of promises when possible
- Minimize bundle size with proper imports
- Use TypeScript strict mode for better optimization
- Avoid deep object nesting

## Memory Management

- Dispose of resources properly
- Avoid circular references
- Use WeakMap/WeakSet when appropriate
- Clear event listeners and timers
- Monitor memory usage during development